# Load test: payments capacity on kind

Run 2026-10-28 22:18 UTC: k6 in the cluster, steps of 10,20,30,40,60,90 payments/s, each ramped over 20s and held for 2m, at most 300 concurrent requests.
Background traffic from the traffic generator (10.1 payments/s) is part of the offered rate.
Every figure is server-side (Prometheus), over the last 90s of each hold.
Cluster: kind, 1 control-plane node and 3 workers (one CDE) sharing a 6-CPU, 9 GB Docker VM.

